Package: lock-input-logger
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         systemd
Description: log which input devices are active while the session is locked
 Root service that follows the logind LockedHint of a user's seat0 session
 and, only while it is locked, logs to the journal which input device
 produced activity and of what coarse kind (typing, key repeat, media key,
 button, pointer). Key codes are never recorded.
 .
 Set LOCK_LOGGER_USER in /etc/default/lock-input-logger, then restart the
 service. Read the log with: journalctl -u lock-input-logger
